.TH GENEEXPRESSION 1 2000-1月 "feature_mean" "feature_mean"
.SH NAME
feature_mean \- Calculate the mean value of one feature row over the given samples.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfeature_mean(\fBexpr\fR as <generic> Matrix, 
\fBfeatureId\fR as string, 
\fBsamples\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Calculate the mean value of one feature row over the given samples.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBexpr\fB \fR\- A gene expression matrix object(the feature could be a gene or a pathway id).. 
.PP
.PP
\fBfeatureId\fB \fR\- The row id of the target feature.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsamples\fB \fR\- 
 A character vector of the sample id for make the column subset of the mean
 calculation, or nothing for using all of the samples in the matrix.
. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
The mean value of the given feature over the selected samples, or \fBNaN\fR when
 the feature id is not found in the given matrix.
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
```r
 let scores = GSVA::gsva(expr, background);
 let ykb = geneExpression::project(scores, c("YKB_WT_WT_R1", "YKB_WT_WT_R2", "YKB_WT_WT_R3"));
 let mean = geneExpression::feature_mean(ykb, "map00791");
 ```
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
geneExpression
.SH FILES
.PP
